    "text_full": "Skip to Content\n\nPagePlay\n\nGuides\nWhat is a CMS?\nLogging in\nLogging out\nWorking with pages\nWorking with paragraphs\nWorking with photos\nAdd downloadable files\nWorking with your Photobanner\nSite statistics (via Google Analytics)\nYour PagePlay email\nAdding new email accounts\nEmail account limit\nSetting up your email account\nArchiving your old emails\nReset an email account password\nSet an out of office message\nBuy a new domain\nShould you drop the www?\nAdding more users who can edit content\nSupported browsers\nUpdate your mail servers\nSearch engines\nSearch Engine Optimisation tips\nGoogle Search console Verification\nFacebook Like Box / Button\nOpening links in new tabs/windows\nReferrer terms and conditions\nHow do I add a file to my site which visitors can then download?\n\nWhether it's a PDF brochure, a sound file or a technical document you want to share with your visitors, we understand that adding downloadable files to the site is important.\n\n1. Click to insert an item\n2. Click 'File'\n\nA file browser window showing you the contents of your computer will appear.\n\n3. Find the file on your computer\n4. Click to upload the file\n\nOnce the file is uploaded you will have the option of naming the file. It will initially be given a name based on the one it already has on your computer - but you may change this for your website.\n\nhelp@pageplay.com\n\n© PagePlay Limited, 2026 - Simple Content Management by PagePlay\n\nCookie policy"
